yz: $14.4B and $5.2B), mainly because so much of Solana's supply hasn't been sold yet \u2014 see the next point."},{"key":"inventory","viz":{"label":"Share of minted supply still with issuers","fmt":"pct","solana":60.59030872282488,"ethereum":17.361765816908346},"title":"Most tokens minted on Solana are still sitting with their issuers","body":"Of $5.9B minted on Solana, $3.6B (61%) is in the issuers' own wallets: created, but not yet bought by anyone. On Ethereum it's 17% ($1.9B of $10.7B). Issuers are listing on Solana ahead of demand, so a token being available there doesn't mean anyone holds it."},{"key":"stocks","viz":{"label":"Tokenised stocks & ETFs held","fmt":"usd","solana":668006986.8741885,"ethereum":702581034.5343864},"title":"In tokenised stocks, Solana is level with Ethereum","body":"$668M of tokenised stocks and ETFs are held on Solana and $703M on Ethereum. It's the only asset class where the smaller chain keeps pace."},{"key":"funds","viz":{"label":"Treasury & money-market funds held","fmt":"usd","solana":424181790.7956755,"ethereum":3487280545.5399976},"title":"Funds and gold are overwhelmingly on Ethereum","body":"Tokenised treasury and money-market funds: $3.5B on Ethereum, $0.4B on Solana. Gold and commodities: $4.8B against $36M. Private credit is closer ($608M against $364M), and on Solana 72% of it is one issuer, OnRe."},{"key":"reach","viz":{"label":"Wallets holding tokenised assets","fmt":"count","solana":1085759,"ethereum":298183},"title":"Solana reaches more people, with much smaller holdings","body":"1.1M wallets hold tokenised assets on Solana, against 298K on Ethereum (rwa.xyz). Divided by what's held, that's about $1,374 per wallet on Solana and $32,078 on Ethereum. Solana is where small holders are; Ethereum is where the money is."},{"key":"defi","viz":{"label":"Share of tokenised value used in DeFi","fmt":"pct","solana":34.5,"ethereum":15.5},"title":"Tokens on Solana are used more in DeFi","body":"34% of Solana's tokenised value is 